  "description": "A fast breakdown of The Hypothalamus: Master of Survival for builders.",
  "is_free": false,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "You're hungry, thirsty, hot, or tired—your hypothalamus noticed before you did.",
      "visual": "🌡️"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "Tiny but powerful, it sits below the thalamus and regulates body temperature, hunger, thirst, and sleep.",
      "visual": "⚖️"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "It commands the pituitary gland, making it the bridge between the nervous system and hormones.",
      "visual": "🌉"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "Damage here can make someone unable to feel full, leading to life-threatening overeating.",
      "visual": "🍔"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "It also controls the stress response, telling adrenal glands when to flood cortisol.",
      "visual": "😰"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "Your survival instincts have a headquarters. It's the hypothalamus.",
      "visual": "🏛️"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "What gland does the hypothalamus directly control?",
    "options": [
      "The pituitary gland",
      "The thyroid gland",
      "The pineal gland"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
